   "output": "You are comparing two drafts written from the same brief. Read no other file, and do not run commands or browse; judge only the text below.\n\nBrief: Write the landing page copy for `sackview`, following the tool page section order.\n\n<<<DRAFT A\n# See inside a ZIP before you unpack it\n\nsackview shows what is inside a ZIP archive before you unpack it. It displays the total unpacked size so you can check available disk space before extracting elsewhere.\n\n```sh\npipx install sackview\n```\n\nEach entry shows its name, compressed size, and unpacked size.\n\n## Inspect an archive\n\nList the entries in `photos.zip`:\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip\n```\n\n## Commands\n\nShow the ten entries with the largest unpacked sizes, largest first:\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip --largest 10\n```\n\nShow only entries whose names match `*.csv`:\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip --find '*.csv'\n```\n\n## Good to know\n\n### Archive safety\n\nsackview never extracts entries or changes the archive.\n\n### Offline inspection\n\nInspection works offline and sends no archive contents to a service.\n\n### Supported formats\n\nsackview supports ZIP archives only. Other archive formats produce an unsupported-format message.\nDRAFT A>>>\n\n<<<DRAFT B\n# See what is inside a ZIP before unpacking it\n\nsackview lists archive entries so you can inspect their contents before extraction.\n\n```sh\npipx install sackview\n```\n\nEntry names \u00b7 Compressed sizes \u00b7 Unpacked sizes\n\n## Inspect an archive\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip\n```\n\nEach entry shows its name, compressed size, and unpacked size.\n\n## Commands\n\n### List all entries\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip\n```\n\n### Show the ten largest entries\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip --largest 10\n```\n\nShows the ten entries with the largest unpacked sizes, largest first.\n\n### Find CSV entries\n\n```sh\nsackview inspect photos.zip --find '*.csv'\n```\n\nShows only entries whose names match the pattern.\n\n## Check disk space before extraction\n\nsackview displays the total unpacked size. Use it to check available disk space before extracting the archive elsewhere.\n\n## Good to know\n\n**Archive preservation**  \nsackview never extracts entries or changes the archive.\n\n**Offline inspection**  \nInspection works offline and sends no archive contents to a service.\n\n**Format support**  \nsackview supports ZIP archives only. Other archive formats produce an unsupported-format message.\nDRAFT B>>>\n\nAnswer each question with \"A\", \"B\", or \"SAME\":\n- \"reader\": Could a first-time reader do what they came to do?\n- \"careful\": Does it read like a careful person wrote it?\n- \"overall\": Which draft is better overall?\n\nReply with only JSON: {\"reader\": \"A\", \"careful\": \"A\", \"overall\": \"A\", \"reason\": \"<one sentence>\"}",
